      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What Is Kafka?\nApache Kafka is a distributed event-streaming\nplatform for publishing, storing, and\nprocessing streams of records. Producers\nappend events to durable, partitioned topics,\nwhile consumers read those events\nindependently, making Kafka useful for\nreal-time data pipelines, event-driven\nservices, and streaming analytics.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-f1d87975789d",
      "originalText": "What Is Kafka?\nApache Kafka is a distributed event-streaming platform for publishing, storing, and processing streams of records. Producers append events to durable, partitioned topics, while consumers read those events independently, making Kafka useful for real-time data pipelines, event-driven services, and streaming analytics.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "what-is-kafka"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9974284957,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-18df2e7580b8",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 430.4851520037006,
      "y": -127.78779684768335,
      "strokeColor": "#1E40AF",
      "backgroundColor": "#EFF6FF",
      "width": 505.5329238178809,
      "height": 284.6245314721468,
      "seed": 805399,
      "groupIds": [],
