      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Application Uses Event\nThe consumer can trigger an alert, perform a calculation, or use a\nsink to write the data to another system. Reading advances the\nconsumer's position but does not delete the Kafka record;\nretention still controls when Kafka removes it.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 16.25,
      "containerId": "node-c0a4a805ee26",
      "originalText": "Application Uses Event\nThe consumer can trigger an alert, perform a calculation, or use a sink to write the data to another system. Reading advances the consumer's position but does not delete the Kafka record; retention still controls when Kafka removes it.",
